{"name":"Shetland","hex":"#c99b5f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shetland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of the Shetland Islands: an archipelago and council area of Scotland.","A historical county of Scotland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A particular breed of pony.","A pony of this breed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shetland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shetland","blocks":[{"text":"Shetland, also called the Shetland Islands, is an archipelago in Scotland lying between Orkney, the Faroe Islands, and Norway, marking the northernmost region of the United Kingdom. The islands lie about 50 miles to the northeast of Orkney, 110 mi (170 km) from mainland Scotland, and 140 mi (220 km) west of Norway."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Flag_of_Shetland.svg/330px-Flag_of_Shetland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shetland","wikidata":"Q47134"},{"title":"Shetland (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Shetland is a British crime drama television series produced by ITV Studios for BBC Scotland. First broadcast on BBC One on 10 March 2013, it is originally based upon the novels of Ann Cleeves and adapted by David Kane. Douglas Henshall starred as DI Jimmy Pérez in the first seven series, while Ashley Jensen portrayed DI Ruth Calder from the eighth series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/Shetland_%28TV_series%29_titlecard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shetland_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q16934235"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/08/Coat_of_arms_of_Shetland.png/120px-Coat_of_arms_of_Shetland.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/08/Coat_of_arms_of_Shetland.